.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH batten-land 1  batten 
.SH NAME
batten\-land \- The landing lap: replay this branch onto a base that moved
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbatten land\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
The landing lap: replay this branch onto a base that moved
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
batten\-land\-replay(1)
Advance the base and replay this branch onto it, recording the outcome
.TP
batten\-land\-wait(1)
Ask whether this head is green and whether its base still holds; the first answer decides
.TP
batten\-land\-push(1)
Push this branch to its own ref, under receive\-pack\*(Aqs compare\-and\-swap
.TP
batten\-land\-verify(1)
Run the configured gate over this head and record what it answered
.TP
batten\-land\-fast\-forward(1)
Ask this head\*(Aqs pull request to fast\-forward, and read the answer that request got
.TP
batten\-land\-lap(1)
Drive the whole lap and lap again on any refusal a rebase would clear
.TP
batten\-land\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
